<title>JAPAN: Japan Aug industrial output down revised 2.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Aug industrial output down revised 2.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in August fell a revised 2.3 percent from the previous month, compared with a preliminary estimate of a 1.9 percent drop, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of the figures follows:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted month on month (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>			   AUG     PRELIM   MONTH AGO   AUG INDEX</p>
<p> Output		 - 2.3    - 1.9   + 4.9	 96.3</p>
<p> Shipments	    - 2.3    - 1.8   + 4.1	 97.5</p>
<p> Inventories	  + 0.8    + 0.6   - 1.2	108.7</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p> Shipments ratio    + 1.3    + 0.9   - 4.2	116.9</p>
<p>Unadjusted year on year (in pct):</p>
<p>				    AUG	PRELIM     MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			  + 1.8     + 2.2     + 6.0</p>
<p> Shipments		     + 1.3     + 1.8     + 6.7</p>
<p> Inventories		   + 1.6     + 1.4     + 1.1</p>
<p>Inventories to  Shipments ratio	     + 0.4	 0.0     - 3.7</p>
</text>
